    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0062" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890.00/7–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-23T19:00:00+01:00">July 23, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 23—6:05 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2910. Bevin has informed me that he is very willing that British and US officials
                    should consult together on the problems dealt with in Deptel 2516, July 20 and
                    Embtel 2881, July 22. He suggests that <pb facs="0063" n="53" xml:id="pg53"/>
                    these talks be carried on while he is away and that when he comes back he will
                    look into the question further with me. Will keep you advised. Is this what you
                    wish?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
